# Own-wording spells of Deep Magic (2014 rules), chunk c (Caustic Touch to Crushing Trample). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Caustic Touch": ["Melee spell attack deals 1d8 acid damage. A target that is concentrating has disadvantage on its concentration save.",
 "Touch. Your hand becomes coated in a film of caustic slime. Make a melee spell attack against a creature you touch. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 acid damage. If the target is concentrating on a spell, it has disadvantage on the Constitution save to keep that concentration.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** The damage increases by 1d8 at 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8) and 17th level (4d8)."],
"Caustic Waste": ["Range 120 ft. A pool of acid deals 4d10 acid damage on entering or ending a turn in it (Dex save for half). +1d10 per slot level above 4.",
 "Range 120 ft, 1 minute. You create a pool of acid in an open space you can see within range. It is either a rectangle 50 feet long, 10 feet wide and 5 feet deep, or a circle 20 feet across and 3 feet deep. Each creature in the area when you cast the spell takes 4d10 acid damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save. A creature that enters the area on its turn or ends its turn there takes the same damage and can make the same save. A creature takes this damage only once per turn.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d10 for each slot level above 4."],
"Cave Dragon's Dominance": ["Take on a cave dragon's traits for 1 minute: AC 16 minimum, poison resistance, two claw attacks, 40 ft climb, blindsight 60 ft and a poison breath three times.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You take on the traits of an adult cave dragon and grow protective scales and claws. For the duration your AC can't be lower than 16 whatever armor you wear, and you have resistance to poison damage. You also gain a climbing speed of 40 feet and blindsight out to 60 feet.\n\nAs an action you can attack twice with your claws. Each is a melee spell attack that deals 1d6 slashing damage plus your spellcasting ability modifier on a hit.\n\nUp to three times while the spell lasts, you can use an action to breathe a 20-foot cone of poison gas. Each creature in the cone takes 6d8 poison damage and is poisoned until it finishes a short rest. A creature that succeeds on a Constitution save takes half as much damage and is not poisoned."],
"Celebration": ["Ritual only. Creatures in a 30 ft radius that fail a Wisdom save fall into carefree revelry and are reluctant to leave. 1 hour.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour, ritual only. You choose a point within range. Around it you create an area with a 30-foot radius. An intelligent creature that enters the area or starts its turn there makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it joins in celebratory revelry such as drinking, singing, laughing and dancing, and it is reluctant to leave until the spell ends. It drops its appointments and worries and acts in a friendly, indulgent way, whatever its agenda or alignment. Assassins stall, servants party instead of working and guards leave their posts.\n\nThe effect ends on a creature if it is attacked, takes damage or is forced out of the area. A creature that succeeds on its save can come and go freely. A creature that fails its save and is forcibly removed must save again if it returns.\n\n**Group Spellcasting.** If other spellcasters help you cast this spell, it lasts 1 extra hour for each helper, up to a total of 3 hours.\n\n**Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, an intelligent creature that has not been affected must save every time it starts its turn in the area, even if it succeeded before."],
"Celestial Fanfare": ["Range 100 ft. Evil creatures in a 30 ft radius take 4d6 thunder and 4d6 radiant damage and are blinded and deafened for 2d4 rounds. Con save reduces. Neutral creatures take half.",
 "Range 100 ft. A great blare of trumpets from on high crashes down on an area you designate. All evil creatures in a 30-foot radius take 4d6 thunder damage and 4d6 radiant damage, and they are blinded and deafened for 2d4 rounds. A successful Constitution save halves the damage and halves the duration of the blinded and deafened conditions.\n\nNeutral or unaligned creatures in the area take half as much damage and are blinded and deafened for half as many rounds. If such a creature succeeds on its save, it takes one-quarter damage and avoids the blinded and deafened conditions. Good creatures are not harmed."],
"Chains of Perdition": ["Range 60 ft. Chains restrain a creature (Dex save) and deal 2d8 bludgeoning plus 2d8 psychic damage each round on your turn. Escape by a Str or Dex check against your DC.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. Iron chains appear near a creature you choose within range. The target makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it is restrained by the chains and takes 2d8 bludgeoning damage and 2d8 psychic damage. It takes the same damage on your turn every round it stays restrained.\n\nOn its turn, a restrained creature can make a Strength or Dexterity check (its choice) against your spell save DC to free itself. The chains remain until the spell ends. While they hold no creature, you can use a bonus action to point them at the same or another creature, moving them up to 20 feet if needed, but if they move beyond the spell's range the spell ends.\n\nThe chains can be destroyed. Treat them as an object with AC 18 and 15 hit points, with resistance to piercing damage and immunity to poison and psychic damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The bludgeoning damage and the psychic damage each increase by 1d8 for every two slot levels above 3."],
"Chains of Torment": ["Self, dim light 10 ft. A chain grapples and restrains a creature within 30 ft (Dex save), dealing 4d6 psychic damage each turn. You can pull one fact from its mind. +1d6 per slot level above 4.",
 "Self, 1 minute. An aura of dim light fills a 10-foot radius around you as you conjure an iron chain that reaches a creature you can see within 30 feet. The creature makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it is grappled (escape DC equals your spell save DC) and also restrained while grappled. A creature that is restrained at the start of its turn takes 4d6 psychic damage. You can restrain only one creature at a time.\n\nAs an action, you can probe the mind of the restrained creature. If it fails a Wisdom save, you learn one specific piece of information it knows, of your choice, such as a name, a password or an important number. The effect does no other harm.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The psychic damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 4."],
"Chains of the Goddess": ["Range 90 ft. A creature that fails a Wisdom save is restrained and takes 6d8 bludgeoning damage, and again at the start of each of your turns. It repeats the save each turn.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 minute. Choose a creature you can see within range. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is restrained by chains of psychic force and takes 6d8 bludgeoning damage. A restrained creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. While it remains restrained, it also takes 6d8 bludgeoning damage at the start of each of your turns."],
"Champion's Weapon": ["Bonus action. A spectral melee weapon of your choice deals force damage and you are proficient with it. +1d8 force per slot level above 2.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. A spectral copy of a melee weapon of your choice appears in your hand. It uses the normal statistics for a weapon of its kind, but it deals force damage instead of its usual type and sheds dim light in a 10-foot radius. You are proficient with it for the duration. Only you can wield it. The spell ends if another creature holds the weapon or if you start your turn more than 10 feet from it.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The weapon deals an extra 1d8 force damage for each slot level above 2."],
"Channel Fiendish Power": ["Self, 10 minutes. Gain two fiendish gifts of your choice, such as fire immunity, spell advantage, weapon resistance, claws or 60 ft wings. One more gift per slot level above 5.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You draw on dark power from the Lower Planes. Your body takes on small fiendish features such as scales, red or green skin or little horns. For the duration you gain two of the following benefits, of your choice.\n\n- Darkvision out to 120 feet that works even in magical darkness.\n- Immunity to fire damage.\n- Immunity to poison damage and the poisoned condition.\n- Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n- Resistance to one of these damage types: cold, fire or lightning.\n- Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from weapons that aren't silvered.\n- Resistance to bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage from nonmagical weapons.\n- Claws that give you a melee weapon attack dealing 1d8 slashing damage.\n- Wings that give you a flying speed of 60 feet.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You choose one additional benefit for each slot level above 5."],
"Chaotic Form": ["Touch, 10 minutes. A willing creature turns ooze-like: ignores difficult terrain, advantage on Acrobatics to escape grapples, squeezes through smaller spaces, but its speed is halved. +10 minutes per slot level above 4.",
 "Touch, 10 minutes. You make the body of a willing creature fluid, so that it drips and flows at its own will like a vaguely humanoid ooze. The creature is not slowed by difficult terrain, has advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks to escape a grapple, and suffers no penalty when squeezing through a space one size smaller than itself. Its movement is halved while the spell lasts.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The duration increases by 10 minutes for each slot level above 4."],
"Chaotic Vitality": ["Melee spell attack on a creature with Hit Dice up to your level. Roll d100 on the Hit Point Flux table to set both your hit points and its. +2 max Hit Dice per slot level above 2.",
 "Touch. Make a melee spell attack against a creature that has at least 1 hit point and no more Hit Dice than your level. On a hit, waves of chaotic energy pulse through the creature and you. After a moment that seems to last forever, both your hit point totals change. Roll a d100, add or subtract any number up to your spellcasting level, and find the result on the Hit Point Flux table. Apply that result to you and to the target. Hit points gained above a creature's normal maximum are temporary hit points that last 1 round per caster level.\n\n**Hit Point Flux.** On 1 to 9 you each have 0 hit points. On 10 to 39 you each have 1. On 40 to 69 you each have 25 percent of the combined total. On 70 to 84 you each have 50 percent. On 85 to 94 you each have 75 percent. On 95 to 99 you each have 100 percent. On a 100 you each have 200 percent of the total and both gain the effect of haste for 1 round per caster level.\n\nExample: a 3rd-level caster with 17 of 30 hit points targets a creature with 54 hit points and rolls 75. Together they have 71 hit points. The result of 50 percent gives each of them 35, and 5 of the caster's 35 are temporary and last 3 rounds.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The maximum Hit Dice of the target increases by 2 for each slot level above 2."],
"Chaotic World": ["Range 60 ft. Enemies in a 30 ft cube must pass an Int save or be blinded, deafened and prone. They can't recover while inside.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. You toss colored cloth into the air and shout disjointed phrases. A 30-foot cube centered on a point within range fills with colored light, loud noise, strong smells and other confusing sensations. Each enemy in the cube makes an Intelligence save. On a failure it is blinded and deafened and falls prone. An affected enemy can't stand up or recover from the blindness or deafness while it stays in the area. All three conditions end at once for a creature that leaves the area."],
"Charm of Great Fondness": ["Range 30 ft. A humanoid that fails a Wisdom save becomes fond of you and tries to charm you back. 1 hour. +1 target per slot level above 2.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 hour. You try to charm a humanoid you can see within range. It makes a Wisdom save, with advantage if you or your companions are fighting it or if you are not of its species. On a failed save, it becomes fond of you until the duration ends or until you or a companion does something harmful to it. The charmed creature sees you as a possible romantic partner and tries to win you over in a way fitting for its kind. It might tell jokes, give a modest gift, flirt gently, show off its strength or compose a love poem. When the spell ends, the creature knows you charmed it.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 2. The targets must be within 30 feet of each other. If two or more of them fail their saves, they squabble among themselves over who deserves your affection more."],
"Charm of Long Standing": ["Works like charm person, but it lasts one day per level you have in your spellcasting class. While it lasts, you are also charmed by the target.",
 "Range 30 ft. This works like charm person, with a longer duration. The target stays charmed for one day for each level you have in your spellcasting class. While the target remains charmed by you, you are also charmed by it, and you won't tolerate any harm, abuse or mistreatment directed at it."],
"Cherub's Burning Blade": ["Self, 10 minutes. A holy fire sword hits for 2d6 fire plus 2d6 radiant damage. A critical hit sets the target aflame for 2d6 fire damage per turn. +1d6 of each per two slot levels above 4.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. A sword of holy fire blazes in your hand. You shape the blade as you wish, but it is never larger than a one-handed weapon made for a Medium creature. If you let go, it vanishes, but while you concentrate you can call it back as a bonus action.\n\nAs an action, you can make a melee attack with the blade. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 fire damage and 2d6 radiant damage. On a critical hit the target catches fire, and until someone uses an action to put out the flames, it takes 2d6 fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The blade sheds bright light in a 10-foot radius and dim light for another 10 feet.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The fire damage and the radiant damage each increase by 1d6 for every two slot levels above 4."],
"Chilling Words": ["Range 30 ft. Mark a creature with a phrase. You and allies can later speak it to freeze it (1d6 psychic, restrained 1 round). A final utterance deals 4d6 psychic damage.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 hour. You speak a short phrase and designate a creature within range. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it becomes vulnerable to the phrase for the duration.\n\nAt any later time while the spell lasts, you and any allies who were within range when you cast it can use an action to speak the phrase, which makes the target freeze in fear. Each of you can use the phrase against the target only once, and the target must be within 30 feet of the speaker. When the target hears it, it must succeed on a Constitution save or take 1d6 psychic damage and be restrained for 1 round. Whether it succeeds or fails, it can't be affected by the phrase again for 1 minute.\n\nYou can end the spell early by speaking the phrase a final time, even if you used it on this target before. When the target hears this last utterance, it takes 4d6 psychic damage and is restrained for 1 minute. With a successful Constitution save, it takes half the damage and is restrained for 1 round."],
"Chronal Lance": ["Range 60 ft. Up to three creatures that fail a Wisdom save have halved speed and disadvantage on Dex checks. They repeat the save each turn. +1 target per slot level above 1.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. You age up to three creatures within range, leaving them briefly sluggish and looking elderly. Each target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, its walking speed is halved (round up to a multiple of 5 feet) and it has disadvantage on Dexterity checks, though not on saving throws. An affected creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1."],
"Circle of Devastation": ["Range 1 mile. A 20 ft radius, 10 ft tall cylinder of energy deals 6d6 damage of a type you pick each turn (Con save for half). It grows by 20 ft each turn.",
 "Range 1 mile, 1 minute. You create a cylinder of destructive energy, 10 feet tall with a 20-foot radius, around a point you can see within range. The area is difficult terrain. When you cast the spell, and as a bonus action on each of your turns, you choose one damage type: cold, fire, lightning, necrotic or radiant. Each creature or object that is in the cylinder when it appears, or that ends its turn there, takes 6d6 damage of the chosen type, or half as much on a successful Constitution save. A creature or object reduced to 0 hit points by the spell turns to fine ash.\n\nAt the start of each of your turns after you cast the spell, the cylinder's radius grows by 20 feet. Creatures and objects caught in the larger area are affected at once."],
"Circle of Wind": ["Self, 8 hours. Gain +2 AC against ranged attacks and advantage on saves against extreme heat, harmful gases, vapors and inhaled poisons.",
 "Self, 8 hours. A light wind swirls around you and leaves you at the center of a mild vortex. For the duration you gain a +2 bonus to AC against ranged attacks. You also have advantage on saving throws against extreme environmental heat and against harmful gases, vapors and inhaled poisons."],
"Claim Lair": ["Touch, 10 minutes. Using 2,000 gp of wealth, claim a lair of up to 2,500 sq ft for 24 hours and use dragon lair actions on initiative 20.",
 "Touch, 24 hours. You place your personal wealth in an area and invoke a dragon's territorial nature, claiming the area as your lair and gaining extra power there. The claimed area can be up to 2,500 square feet (50 feet square, or one hundred 5-foot squares, or twenty-five 10-foot squares) and up to 20 feet tall, shaped as you like. The casting needs material goods and wealth worth at least 2,000 gp.\n\nWhile you are inside, you can take one of these lair actions once per round on initiative count 20.\n\n- **Darkness.** Magical darkness spreads from a point you choose within 30 feet and fills a 15-foot-radius sphere until you dismiss it with an action, use this lair action again, or die. It spreads around corners. Creatures with darkvision can't see through it and nonmagical light can't light it, but you see in it as if it were brightly lit. If it overlaps an area of light made by a spell of 2nd level or lower, that spell is dispelled.\n- **Cave-in.** Part of the ceiling collapses above one creature you can see within 60 feet. It makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC. On a failure it takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage, is knocked prone and is buried. A buried creature is restrained and can't breathe or stand. It can use an action to make a DC 10 Strength check and end the buried state on a success.\n- **Tremor.** A tremor shakes the lair in a 30-foot radius around you. Each creature other than you that is on the ground there makes a Dexterity save against your spell save DC or is knocked prone.\n\nIf you cast this spell on the same area every day for a year, it becomes permanent."],
"Clash of Glaciers": ["Range 100 ft. Icy boulders crush a 100 ft line for 5d6 bludgeoning plus 5d6 cold damage (Dex save for half). +1d6 per slot level above 5.",
 "Range 100 ft. You conjure icy boulders that crush creatures in a line 100 feet long. Each creature in the line takes 5d6 bludgeoning damage and 5d6 cold damage, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 5. You decide whether each extra die deals bludgeoning or cold damage."],
"Claws of Darkness": ["Self, 1 minute. Shadow claws with 10 ft reach let you make melee spell attacks for 1d10 cold damage.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You shape shadows into claws that grow from your fingers and drip black ink. The claws have a reach of 10 feet. For the duration, you can make a melee spell attack with them that deals 1d10 cold damage.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** The spell follows the usual cantrip scaling for damage, if any is listed for it in the source."],
"Claws of the Earth Dragon": ["Range 60 ft. A ray slams a target prone for 6d8 bludgeoning damage (Str save for half and no fall). +1d8 damage and +10 ft range per slot level above 5.",
 "Range 60 ft. You call on the power of an earth dragon and fire a ray at one target within range. The target falls prone and takes 6d8 bludgeoning damage from being slammed to the ground. If it was flying or levitating, it takes an extra 1d6 bludgeoning damage for every 10 feet it falls. On a successful Strength save, the damage is halved, the target doesn't fall and it isn't knocked prone.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d8 and the range increases by 10 feet for each slot level above 5."],
"Clearing the Field": ["Ritual only. Every tree, shrub and stump within 40 ft sinks into the ground for 1 hour, removing cover and difficult terrain.",
 "Range 40 ft, 1 hour, ritual only. With a harsh word and a chopping gesture, you make every tree, shrub and stump within 40 feet of you sink into the ground. The area is left clear of plants that would hinder movement or block sight. Overgrown ground that was difficult terrain becomes clear. The plants rise again as they were when the spell ends or is dispelled. Plant creatures are not affected.\n\n**Group Spellcasting.** If other spellcasters help you cast this spell, it lasts 1 extra hour for each helper, up to a total of 8 hours.\n\n**Ritual Focus.** If you expend your ritual focus, plant creatures in the area must succeed on a Constitution save or be affected as if by enlarge/reduce."],
"Cloak of Fiendish Menace": ["Self, 1 minute. Creatures that come within 5 ft must pass a Wisdom save or be frightened. If you damage a frightened creature it must flee.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You wrap yourself in a menacing fiendish aura. When a creature comes within 5 feet of you, it makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it becomes frightened. A frightened creature makes another save at the start of each of its turns. On a success, it is no longer frightened and can't be frightened again by this casting.\n\nIf you deal damage to a creature frightened by this spell, on its next turn it must take the Dash action and move away from you by the safest route, unless it has nowhere to go. It can't move toward you again while the spell lasts unless it succeeds on a save against the spell."],
"Cloak of Serpents": ["Self, 10 minutes. Gain poison resistance and poison immunity to the poisoned condition. Melee attackers who hit you take 2d8 poison damage and risk being poisoned.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. A mass of writhing, see-through snakes drapes your body to guard you and hold off enemies. You can end the spell early by using an action to dismiss it. For the duration you have resistance to poison damage and immunity to the poisoned condition.\n\nWhenever a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack, a serpent strikes it. The attacker takes 2d8 poison damage and must make a Constitution save or be poisoned for 1 minute. A successful save halves the damage and avoids the poisoned condition."],
"Cloak of Shadow": ["Bonus action, 1 minute. Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks against creatures that rely on sight.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You wrap yourself in shadow. For the duration you have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks against creatures that rely on sight."],
"Cloak of Vermin": ["Self, 10 minutes. A cloak of insects gives +1 AC and deals 2d4 piercing damage to melee attackers. As a bonus action it can leave you as a swarm to attack an adjacent foe.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You conjure a writhing garment of living insects that protects you and harms your foes. While the spell lasts you gain a +1 bonus to AC. Whenever a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack, the insects lash out and deal 2d4 piercing damage to the attacker.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can order the cloak to leave your body as a swarm of insects and enter the space of an adjacent foe. The swarm attacks that foe until you use a bonus action to call it back, the foe moves more than 5 feet away from you, the spell ends, or the swarm dies. You lose the cloak's protection while it is out as a swarm."],
"Clockwork Bodyguard": ["Range 60 ft. Summon clockwork allies of your choice: one huntsman, two hounds or four watchmen. More creatures at slots 6 to 8.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You summon clockwork minions that fight for you. Choose one of these options (see Tome of Beasts, pages 62 to 65, for statistics): one clockwork huntsman, two clockwork hounds, or four clockwork watchmen.\n\nThe clockwork creatures are friendly to you and your companions for the duration. Roll initiative for them, and they take their own turns. They obey your spoken commands (no action required). If you give no commands, they defend themselves and you against hostile creatures but take no other actions. They vanish when they drop to 0 hit points or when the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** More creatures of your choice appear: twice as many with a 6th-level slot, three times as many with a 7th-level slot, and four times as many with an 8th-level slot."],
"Clockwork Bolt": ["Make a ranged weapon attack with a bow or crossbow. If it hits, spinning blades deal an extra 1d8 slashing damage at the end of the target's next turn unless removed.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 round. You imbue an arrow or crossbow bolt with clockwork magic as you fire it. As part of the casting action, you make a ranged weapon attack with a bow or crossbow against one creature within range. On a hit, the missile stays embedded in the target. Unless the target, or an ally of it within 5 feet, uses an action to pull out the missile (which deals no extra damage), spinning blades sprout from it and the target takes an extra 1d8 slashing damage at the end of its next turn. After that, the missile turns back into ordinary ammunition.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** At 5th level the ranged attack deals an extra 1d8 slashing damage on a hit, and the embedded missile's blades deal 1d8 more (2d8 in total) if it isn't removed. Both amounts increase by another 1d8 at 11th level and again at 17th level."],
"Closing In": ["Range 30 ft. A creature that fails a Wisdom save believes the world is crushing it, with disadvantage on checks and attacks and 2d6 psychic damage each turn. +1 target per slot level above 3.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. Choose a creature you can see within range. It makes a Wisdom save, with disadvantage if it is in an enclosed space. On a failure it believes the world around it is closing in to crush it. Even in open ground it feels as if it is sinking into a pit or as if the land is rising around it. For the duration, the creature has disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls and takes 2d6 psychic damage at the end of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 3."],
"Clumsiness": ["Range 30 ft. On a failed Con save, the creature's next Dexterity check subtracts 1d6, and then the spell ends.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 minute. You make a creature within range briefly clumsy. If the target succeeds on a Constitution save, the spell has no effect. On a failure, the next time before the spell ends that the creature makes a Dexterity check, it rolls a d6 and subtracts the result from the check. The spell then ends."],
"Cobra Fangs": ["Touch, 1 minute. The target grows a fanged bite (d4 piercing, plus 3d6 poison on a failed Con save). Magical at slot 3 and higher.",
 "Touch, 1 minute. The target grows long snake fangs. An unwilling creature makes a Wisdom save to avoid the effect. The spell fails if the target already has a bite attack that deals poison damage. If the target has no bite attack, it gains one. The target is proficient with the bite and adds its Strength modifier to the attack and damage rolls. The bite deals piercing damage with a d4 damage die.\n\nWhen the target hits a creature with the bite, that creature makes a Constitution save. It takes 3d6 poison damage on a failure, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a slot of 3rd level or higher, the bite counts as magical for overcoming resistance and immunity to nonmagical attacks and damage."],
"Command Undead": ["Range 60 ft. Undead you can see that fail a Wisdom save follow a one-word command on their next turn. Has no effect on living creatures.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 round. You speak a one-word command to all undead creatures you can see within range. Each target must succeed on a Wisdom save or follow the command on its next turn. The spell has no effect on a target that is alive, doesn't understand your language, or would be directly harmed by the command. See the command spell for typical commands."],
"Compelled Movement": ["Range 60 ft. Two living creatures that fail a Charisma save must move toward each other and fuse when within 5 ft, losing movement and reactions. +1 creature per two slot levels above 3.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. Choose two living creatures (not constructs or undead) you can see within range. Each makes a Charisma save. On a failure, the creature must use its movement to approach the other creature along the most direct route, though it avoids dangerous terrain and enemies. If the two creatures are within 5 feet of each other at the end of either one's turn, their bodies fuse together.\n\nFused creatures still take their own turns, but they can't move or use reactions, and they have disadvantage on attack rolls, Dexterity saves and Constitution checks to hold concentration. A fused creature can use its action to make a Charisma save. On a success, it breaks free and can move normally, but it can fuse again if it is within 5 feet of a creature still under the spell at the end of either creature's turn. The spell doesn't affect a creature that can't be charmed or that is incorporeal.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The number of creatures you can affect increases by one for every two slot levels above 3."],
"Compelling Fate": ["Range 50 ft. A creature that fails a Charisma save is read through the stars: advantage on attacks against it, mirror its movement and warn allies for +2 AC. +1 round per slot level above 3.",
 "Range 50 ft, 1 round. You read a creature you can see through the influence of the stars. If the target fails a Charisma save, you can predict its actions, with these effects.\n\n- You have advantage on attack rolls against the target.\n- For every 5 feet the target moves, you can move 5 feet (up to your normal movement) on the target's turn once it has finished moving. This is deducted from your next turn's movement.\n- As a reaction at the start of the target's turn, you can warn yourself and allies who can hear you of what it intends to do. Any creature targeted by its next attack gains a +2 bonus to AC or to the saving throw against that attack.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The duration increases by 1 round for each slot level above 3."],
"Comprehend Wild Shape": ["Touch, 1 hour. You and a totem holder can understand each other while either is in beast shape. +2 targets per slot level above 2.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. Give one of a matching set of carved totems to an ally and keep another yourself. For the duration, you and the holder of the other totem can understand each other while either of you is in a beast shape. This isn't a telepathic link. You simply understand each other's speech, much like speak with animals. A druid in beast shape still can't cast spells.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can affect two more creatures for each slot level above 2. Each creature must receive a matching carved totem."],
"Confound Senses": ["Range 30 ft. Up to six creatures that fail an Int save have halved speed, disadvantage on ranged attacks and lose their sense of direction.",
 "Range 30 ft, 10 minutes. You befuddle up to six creatures you can see within range so that they see shifting terrain. Each target that fails an Intelligence save has its speed halved until the spell ends because of confusion about its surroundings, and it makes ranged attack rolls with disadvantage. Affected creatures can't keep track of where they are. They automatically fail Wisdom (Survival) checks to avoid getting lost. Whenever an affected creature must choose between paths, it picks at random and immediately forgets which way it came."],
"Conjure Fey Hound": ["Range 60 ft. Summon a hound of the night as a friendly ally for 1 hour. Two hounds at slot 7 and three at slot 9.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You summon a fey hound to fight at your side. A hound of the night (Tome of Beasts, page 251) appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range. The hound vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. It is friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. It obeys your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, it stays by your side and attacks nearby creatures hostile to you but takes no other actions.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a 7th-level slot you summon two hounds. With a 9th-level slot you summon three."],
"Conjure Fiends": ["Range 90 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon fiends of total CR up to 2 as friendly allies for 1 hour. More at slots 6 and 8.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour. You summon fiends that appear in unoccupied spaces you can see within range. Choose one option: one fiend of CR 2 or lower, two fiends of CR 1 or lower, four fiends of CR 1/2 or lower, or eight fiends of CR 1/4 or lower. A summoned fiend vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends.\n\nThe fiends are friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for them as a group, and they take their own turns. They obey your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, they defend themselves against hostile creatures but take no other actions. The GM has the creatures' statistics.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You pick one of the options above and more creatures appear: twice as many with a 6th-level slot and three times as many with an 8th-level slot."],
"Conjure Forest Defender": ["Range 30 ft, 1 hour casting. In a forest, you animate a humanoid body into a forest defender under your control. It is permanent. A 9th-level slot makes two.",
 "Range 30 ft, until dispelled. When you cast this spell in a forest, you bind sticks and twigs around a body, and the body comes to life as a forest defender. It is friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. It obeys your verbal or mental commands (no action required) as long as you stay in its line of sight. If you give no commands, are out of its sight, or are unconscious, it defends itself against hostile creatures but takes no other actions.\n\nThe body used for the spell is destroyed for good and can only be restored to life by true resurrection or wish. You can control only one forest defender at a time. If you cast this spell again, the earlier defender crumbles to dust. The spell consumes one humanoid body as its material component.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a 9th-level slot you summon two forest defenders instead of one and can control up to two at a time."],
"Conjure Greater Spectral Dead": ["Range 60 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon a wraith, spectral guardian or wolf spirit swarm. You command it at the cost of 1d6 psychic damage per turn. It turns on you if concentration breaks.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You summon an incorporeal undead creature that appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range. Choose one option: one wraith, one spectral guardian, or one wolf spirit swarm. The summoned creature vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. The spell requires bone dust, a crystal prism worth at least 100 gp and a platinum coin.\n\nThe creature won't attack you or your companions. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. It attacks your enemies and tries to stay within 60 feet of you, but otherwise controls its own actions. It resents being bound and may harm or hinder you and your companions by any means other than direct attacks.\n\nAt the start of its turn you can use your reaction to command it by voice. It obeys for that turn, and you take 1d6 psychic damage at the end of that turn. If your concentration is broken, the creature doesn't vanish. You can no longer command it, and it becomes hostile to you and your companions. It attacks you if it thinks it can win or do real harm, and flees otherwise. You can't dismiss it, but it disappears 1 hour after you summoned it.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a 9th-level slot you summon a deathwisp or two ghosts instead."],
"Conjure Mantelet": ["Self, 1 minute. A luminous barrier with an arrow slit gives you three-quarters cover and moves with you.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You summon a see-through, faintly glowing barrier with a single arrow slit. For the duration, the mantelet gives you three-quarters cover. If you move on your turn, the mantelet moves with you."],
"Conjure Minor Voidborn": ["Range 90 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon fiends or aberrations of total CR up to 2. They are uncontrolled, you command them at the cost of 1d6 psychic damage. More at slots 7 and 9.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour. You summon fiends or aberrations that appear in unoccupied spaces you can see within range. Choose one option: one creature of CR 2 or lower, two of CR 1 or lower, four of CR 1/2 or lower, or eight of CR 1/4 or lower. They vanish when they drop to 0 hit points or when the spell ends.\n\nThe creatures do not directly attack you or your companions. Roll initiative for them as a group, and they take their own turns. They attack your enemies and try to stay within 90 feet of you, but they control their own actions. They resent being bound, so they may harm or hinder you and your companions with secondary effects, but not with direct attacks.\n\nAt the start of their turn you can use your reaction to command them by voice. They obey on that turn, and you take 1d6 psychic damage at the end of it. If your concentration is broken, the spell ends but the creatures stay. You can no longer command them, and they become hostile to you and your companions. They attack you and your allies if they think they can win or do real harm, but they won't fight if they fear their own death. You can't dismiss them, and they vanish 1 hour after being summoned.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You pick one of the options above and more creatures appear: twice as many with a 7th-level slot and three times as many with a 9th-level slot."],
"Conjure Mock Animals": ["Range 30 ft. As conjure animals, but each beast has 1 hit point, deals 1 damage and explodes for 2d4 radiant damage when it drops to 0, possibly blinding nearby creatures.",
 "Range 30 ft, 10 minutes. You summon fey spirits that look like animals but exist only as a distraction and a trap. The spell works like conjure animals, except that each mock animal has only 1 hit point and deals only 1 damage on a hit, whatever its appearance.\n\nWhen a mock animal drops to 0 hit points, it bursts in a flash of light and deals 2d4 radiant damage to every creature within 5 feet of it. Each creature that takes this damage makes a Dexterity save and is blinded for 1 round on a failure. A bursting mock animal doesn't damage other mock animals."],
"Conjure Nightmare": ["Range 60 ft. Summon a nightmare as a mount for 1 hour. If concentration breaks, it may turn on you unless you gave it a sacrifice. +1 hour per slot level above 5.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You call forth a nightmare to serve you. It appears in an unoccupied space you choose within range and serves as your mount, in combat and out of it. It is friendly to you and your companions for the duration and follows your commands.\n\nIf your concentration is broken, the nightmare is no longer bound. It may leave at once, particularly if it has been hurt or threatened, but it is just as likely to attack you or an ally or otherwise take revenge for being summoned. If you give the nightmare a sacrifice to devour when you first summon it, it is satisfied and simply returns home when the spell ends, without harming you or your companions.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The duration increases by 1 hour for each slot level above 5."],
"Conjure Scarab Swarm": ["Range 60 ft. Two swarms of beetles (swarms of insects) appear as friendly allies for 10 minutes.",
 "Range 60 ft, 10 minutes. You summon swarms of scarab beetles to attack your foes. Two swarms of insects (beetles) appear in unoccupied spaces you can see within range. Each swarm vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. The swarms are friendly to you and your allies. Make one initiative roll for both swarms, and they take their own turns. They obey your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, they defend themselves against hostile creatures but take no other actions."],
"Conjure Shadow Titan": ["Range 90 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon a shadow titan, a stone giant that hides in dim light and hurls shadow rocks for cold damage. Friendly for 1 hour.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour. You summon a shadow titan, which appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range. It uses the statistics of a stone giant with two changes: its camouflage works in dim light instead of rocky terrain, and the rocks it hurls are made of shadow and deal cold damage.\n\nThe titan is friendly to you and your companions. Roll initiative for it, and it acts on its own turn. It obeys your spoken or telepathic commands (no action required). If you give none, it defends itself against hostile creatures but takes no other actions. It vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends."],
"Conjure Spectral Dead": ["Range 60 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon a shroud as a friendly ally for 1 hour. A 3rd-level slot gives two shrouds or a specter, a 4th-level slot or higher gives four shrouds or a will-o'-wisp.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 hour. You summon a shroud (Tome of Beasts, page 348) to do your bidding. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and is friendly to you and your allies for the duration. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. It obeys your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, it defends itself against hostile creatures but takes no other actions. It vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. The spell requires bone dust, a crystal prism and a silver coin.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a 3rd-level slot you can summon two shrouds or one specter. With a slot of 4th level or higher you can summon four shrouds or one will-o'-wisp."],
"Conjure Undead": ["Range 30 ft, 1 minute casting. Summon a shadow as a friendly ally for 1 hour. A 4th-level slot allows a wight, and a 5th-level slot or higher allows a ghost.",
 "Range 30 ft, 1 hour. You summon a shadow to do your bidding. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range and is friendly to you and your allies. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. It obeys your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, it defends itself against hostile creatures but takes no other actions. It vanishes when the spell ends. The spell requires a humanoid skull.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a 4th-level slot you can summon a wight or a shadow. With a slot of 5th level or higher you can summon a ghost, a shadow or a wight."],
"Conjure Voidborn": ["Range 90 ft. Summon a fiend or aberration of CR 6 or lower. You command it at the cost of 2d6 psychic damage. It turns on you if concentration breaks. +1 CR per slot level above 7.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour. You summon a fiend or aberration of challenge rating 6 or lower, which appears in an unoccupied space you can see within range. It vanishes when it drops to 0 hit points or when the spell ends. Roll initiative for it, and it takes its own turns. By default it attacks the nearest creature.\n\nAt the start of its turn you can use your reaction to command it by speaking in Void Speech. It obeys that command, and you take 2d6 psychic damage at the end of its turn. If your concentration is broken, the spell ends but the creature stays. You can no longer command it, and it becomes hostile to you and your companions. It attacks you and your allies if it thinks it can win or do real harm, but won't fight if it fears for its own life. You can't dismiss it, and it vanishes 1 hour after you summoned it.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The challenge rating increases by 1 for each slot level above 7."],
"Consult the Storm": ["Range 90 ft. Ask a storm entity a 15-word question. A booming answer is heard within 600 ft and deals 7d6 thunder damage in a 15 ft radius (Con save for half). +1d6 per slot level above 4.",
 "Range 90 ft. You put a question to an entity tied to storms, such as an elemental, a deity or a primal spirit, and it answers with destructive fury. As part of casting, you speak a question of fifteen words or fewer and choose a point within range. A short, truthful answer booms from that point and can be heard clearly by any creature within 600 feet. Each creature within 15 feet of the point takes 7d6 thunder damage, or half as much on a successful Constitution save.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 4."],
"Contagion": ["Melee spell attack poisons the target. Three failed Con saves at the end of its turns inflict a disease of your choice, three successes end the spell. 7 days.",
 "Touch, 7 days. Your touch spreads disease. Make a melee spell attack against a creature within your reach. On a hit, the target is poisoned. At the end of each of the poisoned target's turns, it makes a Constitution save. If it succeeds on three of these saves, it is no longer poisoned and the spell ends. If it fails three, it is no longer poisoned, and you choose one of the diseases below. The target has that disease for the rest of the duration. Because the spell causes a natural disease, effects that remove or ease disease apply to it.\n\n- **Blinding Sickness.** Pain grips the creature's mind and its eyes turn milky white. It has disadvantage on Wisdom checks and Wisdom saves and is blinded.\n- **Filth Fever.** A raging fever sweeps through the body. The creature has disadvantage on Strength checks, Strength saves and attack rolls that use Strength.\n- **Flesh Rot.** The creature's flesh decays. It has disadvantage on Charisma checks and vulnerability to all damage.\n- **Mindfire.** The creature's mind becomes feverish. It has disadvantage on Intelligence checks and Intelligence saves, and in combat it acts as if under the confusion spell.\n- **Seizure.** The creature shakes uncontrollably. It has disadvantage on Dexterity checks, Dexterity saves and attack rolls that use Dexterity.\n- **Slimy Doom.** The creature bleeds uncontrollably. It has disadvantage on Constitution checks and Constitution saves, and whenever it takes damage it is stunned until the end of its next turn.\n- **Rust.** Symptoms appear in 1d4 days, starting with an itchy rash at the wound. A day later the rash peels off and reveals rusted metal. All effects that restore hit points are halved for the creature, including long rests, so a long rest gives back only half its missing hit points. It still regains spent Hit Dice at the usual rate."],
"Control Ice": ["Range 300 ft. Control ice in a cube up to 100 ft on a side: crack it (4d10 collapse damage), reshape it, or thicken or thin it.",
 "Range 300 ft, 1 minute. You control ice in a cube up to 100 feet on a side within range. When you cast the spell you choose one effect, and as an action on each later turn you can repeat it or pick another. Changes to the ice remain after the spell ends, but other effects (temperature, tremors, another casting of this spell) can alter them.\n\n- **Crack.** The ice cracks and splinters. On level ground it becomes difficult terrain and may cause other hazards, such as a pit under ice over a chasm or floes from ice over water. Using this on ice cliffs, walls or ceilings can bring them down, dealing 4d10 bludgeoning damage to creatures below, or half as much on a successful Dexterity save. The fallen ice becomes difficult terrain.\n- **Reshape.** Ice in part of the area rapidly melts, shifts and re-forms into a shape you command. You can fill holes, open tunnels, form bridges, remove difficult terrain or otherwise change the ice. You can make ice slippery, which makes it difficult terrain, or dry it out to remove difficult terrain. You can fill a hole up to a 20-foot cube, make a bridge 20 feet long and up to 20 feet wide, or raise a pillar 20 feet tall and up to 20 feet square. By repeating this on later turns while you concentrate, you can enlarge the affected area.\n- **Thicken/Thin.** Existing ice becomes thicker or thinner by up to 1 inch per round over some or all of the area, making a surface stronger or turning it into thin, hazardous ice."],
"Converse with Dragon": ["Self, 10 minutes. Telepathy with any dragon within 120 ft, whatever languages it speaks. A dragon can resist with a Charisma save.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You gain limited telepathy that lets you communicate with any creature of the dragon type within 120 feet, whatever languages it knows. A dragon can choose to make a Charisma save to block telepathic contact with itself. The spell doesn't change a dragon's attitude toward you or your allies. It only opens a channel, and unwanted contact can sometimes make a dragon think worse of you."],
"Convoluted Dictum": ["Range 60 ft. A creature that fails a Wisdom save can take only one action or bonus action per turn, and spells and object interactions may be delayed on a d20 roll of 11 or higher.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. You twist a creature's thinking within range so that it takes longer, more elaborate steps to do things. The target must succeed on a Wisdom save or be able to take only one action or bonus action on each of its turns until the spell ends.\n\nIf the target tries to cast a spell with a casting time of 1 action, it rolls a d20. On an 11 or higher, the spell doesn't take effect until the target's next turn, and it must use its action on that turn to finish the spell. If it can't, the spell is wasted. If the target handles an object as part of an action, such as drawing a sword as part of an attack, it also rolls a d20. On an 11 or higher, the object interaction becomes its only action that round, using Use an Object. In the sword example, the target spends its action drawing the blade with great flourish and can't attack with it until its next turn.\n\nAt the end of each of its turns, the target can make another Wisdom save, ending the spell on a success."],
"Costly Victory": ["Range 90 ft. Up to ten enemies that fail a Wisdom save burst into flame, taking 6d8 fire and 6d8 radiant damage, if they drop one of your allies to 0 hit points within 1 hour.",
 "Range 90 ft, 1 hour. You choose up to ten enemies you can see within range. Each makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, the creature is cursed to burst into flame if it reduces one of your allies to 0 hit points before the spell ends. When it bursts, it takes 6d8 fire damage and 6d8 radiant damage. If the creature wears flammable material or is made of it (such as a plant creature), it catches fire and keeps burning, taking fire damage equal to your spellcasting ability modifier at the end of each of its turns, until it or an ally within 5 feet of it uses an action to put out the fire."],
"Create Ring Servant": ["Touch, 1 hour. Two metal rings become a ring servant, a friendly construct that obeys spoken commands and reverts to rings at 0 hit points.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You touch two metal rings and fill them with life, creating a short-lived but sentient construct called a ring servant. It appears adjacent to you. When it drops to 0 hit points or the spell ends, it turns back into the rings used to cast the spell. The ring servant is friendly to you and your companions for the duration. Roll initiative for it, and it acts on its own turns. It obeys your spoken commands (no action required). If you give none, it defends itself and you against hostile creatures but takes no other actions."],
"Create Thunderstaff": ["Touch, 10 minutes. After 60 days in a noisy place, a quarterstaff becomes a thunderstaff: a +1 quarterstaff with 10 charges that adds 1d8 thunder damage and can cast thunderwave.",
 "Touch, instantaneous. You cast this spell on an ordinary quarterstaff, which must then be mounted in a noisy place such as a busy marketplace and left there for 60 days. During that time it slowly soaks up ambient sound. After 60 days it is fully charged and can't absorb more, and it becomes a thunderstaff, a +1 quarterstaff with 10 charges.\n\nWhen you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can spend 1 charge to deal an extra 1d8 thunder damage to the target. You can also cast thunderwave from the staff as a bonus action by spending 2 charges. The staff can't be recharged. If the last charge isn't spent within 60 days, the staff becomes nonmagical again."],
"Creeping Darkness": ["Range 60 ft. A mass of shadow fills three 10 ft cubes and creeps 20 ft per round. Creatures it enters take 6d6 necrotic damage and are restrained (Con save for half and not restrained).",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. You create a writhing mass of shadow that moves slowly in a direction you choose. Its grasping tendrils fill up to three 10-foot cubes within range. The mass has a speed of 20 feet and moves at the end of your turn each round, ignoring difficult terrain. It can also move vertically or across a ceiling, provided there is a surface to cling to. All light in the area is reduced to dim light, and the covered ground is difficult terrain.\n\nWhen the darkness moves into a living creature's space, that creature takes 6d6 necrotic damage and is restrained, and it makes a Constitution save. On a success it takes half damage and isn't restrained. A creature in the area at the start of its turn makes another Constitution save and takes damage again each round it remains. Restrained creatures move with the darkness, dragged by the tendrils. A creature can use an action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC to free itself.\n\nBright light can destroy parts of the spell. One 5-foot cube is destroyed if it takes 12 radiant damage. As long as at least one 5-foot cube covers any part of a creature's space, the creature stays restrained."],
"Creeping Ice": ["Range 60 ft. A 5 ft square of ice is difficult terrain and restrains a creature (Str save), dealing 2d6 cold damage each turn. Larger and stronger at higher slots.",
 "Range 60 ft, 1 minute. You create a sheet of ice covering a 5-foot square within range for the duration. The iced area is difficult terrain. A creature in the area when you cast the spell makes a Strength save or is restrained as ice quickly encases it. A restrained creature takes 2d6 cold damage at the start of its turn. It can use an action to make a Strength check against your spell save DC, with disadvantage, to free itself on a success. The creature can also be freed, ending the spell, if the ice takes at least 20 damage. The restrained creature takes half the damage from attacks made against the ice.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a slot of 4th to 6th level, the area becomes a 10-foot square, the ice deals 4d6 cold damage and 40 damage melts each 5-foot square. With a slot of 7th level or higher, the area becomes a 20-foot square, the ice deals 6d6 cold damage and 60 damage melts each 5-foot square."],
"Cruor of Visions": ["Self, 1 minute casting. Pricking your finger makes a pool of blood that works as a crystal ball and a crystal ball of telepathy. Another creature's blood gives it disadvantage on saves against scrying.",
 "Self, 5 minutes. You prick your finger with a bone needle as you cast, taking 1 necrotic damage. The blood must be caught in a container such as a platter or bowl, where it grows into a pool 1 foot across. The pool works as a crystal ball for scrying. If you add a drop, or dried flakes, of another creature's blood to the container, that creature has disadvantage on any Wisdom save to resist the scrying. You can also treat the pool as a crystal ball of telepathy.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a slot of 7th level or higher, the pool acts as a crystal ball of mind reading or a crystal ball of true seeing, as you choose when you cast the spell."],
"Crushing Curse": ["Range 60 ft. A creature that fails a Wisdom save takes 1d6 psychic damage and is deafened for 1 minute, though it still hears Void Speech.",
 "Range 60 ft. You speak a word of Void Speech and choose a creature you can see within range. If the target can hear you, it must succeed on a Wisdom save or take 1d6 psychic damage and be deafened for 1 minute, except that it can still hear Void Speech. A creature deafened this way can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.\n\n**Cantrip Upgrade.** The damage increases by 1d6 at 5th level (2d6), 11th level (3d6) and 17th level (4d6)."],
"Crushing Trample": ["Self, 1 round. Move up to twice your speed in a line, trampling foes of your size or smaller for 4d6 bludgeoning damage and knocking them prone (Str save). No opportunity attacks.",
 "Self, 1 round. You are filled with a desire to run down your foes. You at once move up to twice your speed in a straight line, trampling every enemy in your path that is your size or smaller. If you try to move through the space of an enemy larger than you, your movement and the spell end. Each enemy whose space you pass through makes a Strength save. On a failure it is knocked prone and takes 4d6 bludgeoning damage. If you have hooves, add your Strength modifier (minimum +1) to the damage. You move through enemy spaces whether or not they succeed on their saves. You don't provoke opportunity attacks while moving under this spell."],
}
